From 0014000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex local builder <codex@local.invalid>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 13:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] LOCAL: enable user namespaces for Droidspaces

Enable CONFIG_USER_NS for Docker, Flatpak, Bubblewrap, browsers, and
other sandboxed workloads that create user namespaces. This is intentionally
separate from the previously validated container candidate because enabling
this kernel feature requires a fresh strict ABI/KMI and stock-module audit.

Change-Id: I0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
index 35a79cb4d523..30a3b93d1384 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@ CONFIG_CPUSETS_V1=y
 CONFIG_CGROUP_CPUACCT=y
 CONFIG_CGROUP_BPF=y
 CONFIG_NAMESPACES=y
+CONFIG_USER_NS=y
 CONFIG_RT_SOFTIRQ_AWARE_SCHED=y
 # CONFIG_RD_BZIP2 is not set
 # CONFIG_RD_LZMA is not set

-- 
2.55.0
